WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.050
Laying a course is the most common thing you’ll do on the plotting exam, so let’s make it a routine.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.425
Draw a straight line from your departure point to your destination.

3
00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:12.325
And look along it.

4
00:00:12.575 --> 00:00:15.000
Does it cross land, or a shoal?

5
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:20.650
Walk the parallel rulers to the nearest rose, and read the true course on the outer ring.

6
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.525
Measure the length of the line with your dividers on the latitude scale.

7
00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:29.350
What if the leg is longer than your dividers will open?

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.775
Set them to a round number, say five miles, on the side scale.

9
00:00:35.025 --> 00:00:40.000
Step them along the line, count the steps, and then measure the leftover piece.

10
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.225
Finally, label it.

11
00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.725
Course above, speed below.

12
00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:48.575
And write your estimated time of arrival at the far end.
